  "conclusion": "Mood improves after watching cat videos: positive-emotion composite 3.99 -> 4.76 (+0.77, t(6604) = 51.3, sign-flip p < 1e-5, bootstrap CI [+0.74, +0.80]) and negative-emotion composite 2.19 -> 1.46 (-0.73, t(6593) = 59.0, sign-flip p < 1e-5, bootstrap CI [-0.77, -0.72]). All 7 discrete emotions move in the mood-beneficial direction (|t| = 26.7-78.8, p < .001); energy rises (+0.51) and depletion falls (-1.38). Retrospective self-report, no control group, self-selected snowball sample (88.4% female): supported as a within-person association, not a causal effect."
